# What plugins/browsertabs/init.lua needs, declared beside the file that consumes it. Format
# is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Dependencies.spoon for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# core is not a tool to install, it is a capability the composition root hands this file
# from Olm's own lib, so this line decides injection rather than installation. Optional,
# because only the resting order of the tab list degrades without it, the list still opens
# and still switches tabs.
recency | core | lib/recency.lua | optional | remembering the last opened tab, so the list opens already ordered by that
